Answer: Call  $S = \sum_{i=1}^{n-1} i \alpha^{2i}=\sum_{i=1}^{n-1} i (\alpha^2)^{i}$  and  $\alpha^2 = \beta$ . If  $\beta \neq 1$ , then  \begin{align} \beta S = \sum_{i=1}^{n-1} i \beta^{i+1} &= \sum_{i=1}^{n-1}\left((i+1)-1\right) \beta^{i+1} \\ &=\sum_{i=1}^{n-1} (i+1)\beta^{i+1} - \sum_{i=1}^{n-1} \beta^{i+1} \\ &= \sum_{i=2}^{n}i \beta^{i} - \sum_{i=2}^{n}\beta^{i} \\ &= \left( n\beta^n-\beta \right) +\sum_{i=1}^{n-1}i\beta^{i} - \sum_{i=2}^{n}\beta^{i} \\ &= \left( n\beta^n-\beta \right) + S - \frac{\beta^{n+1} - \beta^2 }{\beta  -1 }
 \end{align} 
 Thus  $$ (\beta - 1)S = n\beta^{n}-\beta - \frac{\beta^{n+1} - \beta^2}{\beta -1 } $$ 
 or  \begin{align} S &= \frac{n\beta^n -\beta}{\beta -1} - \frac{\beta^{n+1} - \beta^2 }{(\beta - 1)^2
} \\ &=\frac{(n-1)\beta^{n+1} - n\beta^n + \beta}{ (\beta - 1)^2} \\& = \frac{(n-1)\alpha^{2n+2} - n\alpha^{2n} + \alpha^2}{ (\alpha^2 - 1)^2} 
\end{align} 
 If  $\beta = \alpha^2 = 1$ , then  $S=\sum_{i=1}^{n-1} i (\alpha^2)^{i} = \sum_{i=1}^{n-1}i=\frac{(n-1)n}{2}$ . 
